index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..04d0f4f8496bad3aee83e825bcb89fab93a28afb
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tools/testing/selftests/authority/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,120 @@
+# Filesystem Authority qualification tests
+
+Run only inside a disposable VM. `qualification_test` creates private mount
+namespaces and mounts; construction of scopes requires CAP_SYS_ADMIN. The
+original `authority_test` contains 13 cases; `qualification_test` contains 22
+**grouped** cases with syscall and stress assertions, not 22 individual syscalls.
+`landlock_fd_test` adds seven differential FD/LSM groups. A skipped ACL or LSM
+precondition is not a pass. All binaries return kselftest status. The targeted
+Landlock audit corrected the old retroactive READ-clone denial expectation and
+added a real cached-TRUNCATE amplification regression. See the qualification
+ledger and Documentation/authority/landlock-audit.md.
+Do not infer general process confinement from these tests.
+
+Additional qualification groups:
+
+* `temporal_test`: fifteen executed temporal FD/context/async/LSM/concurrency
+  groups plus one explicit SKIP for the absent global-revocation API. Distinguishes
+  independent clone ownership, mutable FD aliases, COW task credentials and
+  ring-bound personality snapshots. Native controls also run on pristine Linux.
+  Registration after source reduction must capture the reduced state; an earlier
+  legitimate context may remain valid. Dedicated enforcing LSM fixture sources,
+  policies and exact commands are retained in the temporal-authority report.
+  See Documentation/authority/temporal-semantics.md; stored identity alone does
+  not constitute a delegated Authority capability.
+
+* `idmapped_test`: nine groups covering tmpfs idmap identity/DAC/ACLs, native
+  and UNHANDLED behavior, mount-bound scope ceilings, clone/dup attenuation,
+  create ownership, NOREPLACE/EXCHANGE rename, LINK, unlink, truncate, lifetime,
+  and inability of nested-userns root to manufacture initial-userns scopes.
+* `callback_test`: four native/handled overlayfs groups. Explicit scopes do
+  not override filesystem permission callbacks; unsupported overlay FD-cap
+  operations remain EOPNOTSUPP. This is not general callback-FS qualification.
+* `establishment_test`: eleven grouped pidfd/procfs/O_PATH, fanotify,
+  ordinary io_uring/fixed-file, memfd and SysV boundary checks.
+* `dac_fd_test`: eleven DAC/FSUID/FSGID/group/provider and managed transfer,
+  mmap/mprotect/fallocate/metadata attenuation groups.
+* `handle_test`: twelve generic/XFS handle acquisition groups, including four
+  native controls. Requires a **dedicated disposable** XFS mount at `/mnt/xfs`;
+  otherwise skips before assertions. It creates a unique temporary subdirectory.
+  It does not format disks; guest orchestration must provide the fixture.
+
+Use CONFIG_USER_NS=y, TMPFS_POSIX_ACL=y, OVERLAY_FS=y, FANOTIFY=y and
+FANOTIFY_ACCESS_PERMISSIONS=y for the relevant groups. Namespace/privilege
+prerequisite skips are not passes. Exact evaluated configurations and orchestration
+are recorded in Documentation/authority/qualification-status.md and the final
+closure evidence, including selected major-LSM policies. These new groups are
+invariant-oriented replacements, not recovered copies or numerical equivalents
+of the historical 21/47 harnesses. Registered io_uring credential personalities
+are distinct from ordinary submission or fixed-file imports; the retained
+credential-token observation is not counted as a security PASS.
+
+## External build
+
+Use a clean source snapshot containing **all** intended tracked and untracked
+prototype files. Never run mrproper in the working tree to obtain this snapshot.
+For example, from the tree root, with a NEW `/tmp/authority-repro` directory:
+
+```sh
+E=/tmp/authority-repro
+mkdir -p "$E/src" "$E/build" "$E/tests"
+git ls-files -co --exclude-standard -z | sort -zu |
+  tar --null -T - -cf "$E/source.tar"
+tar -xf "$E/source.tar" -C "$E/src"
+cd "$E/src"
+make O="$E/build" x86_64_defconfig
+scripts/kconfig/merge_config.sh -m -O "$E/build" "$E/build/.config" \
+  tools/testing/selftests/authority/qualification.config
+make O="$E/build" olddefconfig
+make O="$E/build" -j12 bzImage
+make O="$E/build" headers_install INSTALL_HDR_PATH="$E/headers"
+make -C tools/testing/selftests/authority OUTPUT="$E/tests/" \
+  CFLAGS="-static -Wall -O2 -isystem $E/headers/include"
+bash tools/testing/selftests/authority/run-qemu.sh \
+  "$E/build/arch/x86/boot/bzImage" /path/to/busybox-static "$E/run" \
+  "$E/tests/authority_test" "$E/tests/qualification_test" "$E/tests/landlock_fd_test"
+```
+
+Required build tools: GCC, binutils, make, flex, bison, bc, libelf/libssl headers,
+rsync, Python, Perl; guest packaging: cpio/gzip and static BusyBox; runtime:
+QEMU x86_64 and /dev/kvm. Container builds must mount only the staging snapshot
+and evidence, not the worktree. Neither the runner nor the build installs a
+kernel. QEMU has no network interface or host filesystem/block-device export.
+Runner evidence directories must not already exist. `QEMU_TIMEOUT` defaults to
+600 seconds. The console loglevel suppresses informational printk interleaving;
+the guest dumps the full kernel log after suites. Kernel poweroff alone does
+not count as a pass: suite exit markers and kernel diagnostics are checked.
+Review full logs and TAP totals as well. Initramfs ownership and timestamps
+are normalized (SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH, default zero); the kernel build itself is
+not claimed bit-identical without matching build metadata and toolchain.
+
+`QEMU_ASSETS=/directory` copies required companion binaries into each guest
+suite's working directory. For upstream Landlock `base_test` / `fs_test`, build
+its directory with static CFLAGS and include `true`, `sandbox-and-launch`,
+`wait-pipe`, and `wait-pipe-sandbox` as assets. Fresh writable per-suite working
+directories are necessary; running fs_test from `/` collides with `/tmp`.
+
+For KASAN/lockdep merge `debug.config` into a **separate** build. For KCSAN use a
+separate configuration with KASAN disabled and KCSAN/KCSAN_STRICT enabled; check
+that olddefconfig retained the options. For 32-bit compatibility build the same
+userspace sources with `-m32` and multilib libc, then run on the IA32-enabled
+x86_64 guest. This is not a native 32-bit kernel qualification.
+
+To exercise ramfs, compile a second qualification binary with
+`-DTEST_FS='"ramfs"'`; the ACL case must skip if the filesystem lacks POSIX ACLs.
+The read-only subfixture intentionally remains tmpfs. Save source/config,
+compiler versions, all build/run commands, logs and SHA-256 manifests. Fragment
+files describe required features, not bit-identical kernels; use the retained
+full `.config` for an exact configuration reproduction.
+
+There is currently **no Authority enable/disable Kconfig switch**. KUNIT=n only
+disables synthetic tests, not enforcement. Do not describe it as Authority-off.
+Build landlock_fd_test with `-DENABLE_AUTHORITY=0` to leave the task's Authority
+domain unhandled; this does NOT compile out the Authority FD API. The test
+queries Landlock availability and records unsupported subcases as skips. The
+post-open fixture deliberately grants READ of its own executable so execve
+inheritance tests do not fail on the test binary's acquisition itself.
+
+The old temporary 21-case capability and 47-case DAC harnesses are not restored
+by this suite. See Documentation/authority/qualification-status.md and
+filesystem-v1-matrix.md for the release-gate decision and remaining blockers.
